<title>PERU: Peru net reserves fall to $8.391 bln on Sept 11.</title>
<headline>Peru net reserves fall to $8.391 bln on Sept 11.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peru's Central Reserve Bank said on Monday that its net international reserves stood at $8.448 billion on September 11, down from $8.448 billion the week before.</p>
<p>The bank's foreign exchange position, or total liquidity minus short and long-term debt obligations, was $1.740 billion on the same day.</p>
<p>International reserves ended 1995 at $6.641 billion.</p>
<p>-- Saul Hudson, Lima newsroom, 511 221-2134</p>
